The feature set is modelled on ApE (A Plasmid Editor) by M. Wayne Davis. No
ApE code is used or derived from; its feature-library format and GenBank colour
qualifiers are followed so that files move between the two programs. Cite:
    Davis MW, Jorgensen EM (2022). ApE, A Plasmid Editor: A Freely Available DNA
    Manipulation and Visualization Program. Frontiers in Bioinformatics
    2:818619. https://doi.org/10.3389/fbinf.2022.818619

Bisulfite primers (dnakit/bisulfite.py) are rewritten from
design_bisulfite_primers.py v1.1, a later version of a script whose original
header reads:

design_bisulfite_primers v1.0            by Colette L. Picard, 06/05/2016

    The method, its defaults and the score that ranks primer pairs are hers.
    The code here is a new implementation, not a copy, with three fixes listed
    in the module's docstring and on the Help page. The check of each primer
    against a genome, done by the script with BLAST against TAIR10, is done
    here by the Genome Browser (see its NOTICE).

    If primers designed with this tool go into a paper, please credit
    Colette L. Picard's design_bisulfite_primers.py.

